<!-- Research -->
<section id="research">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <h2 class="section-label">Research</h2>
    <div class="research-layout">
      <div>
        <h3 class="research-heading">Resolving Intent-Content Conflict in Retrieval</h3>
        <p class="research-lead">Retrieval systems often equate relevance with topical similarity, even when a user&rsquo;s intended experience conflicts with a topic&rsquo;s usual properties. We formalized this failure mode as intent-content conflict.</p>
        <p class="research-method">I built KRAG, an emotion-aware knowledge graph framework that represents affect as graph evidence, aligns graph representations with Sentence-BERT, and reranks semantic candidates using topical, relational, and affective signals.</p>
        <p class="research-method">KRAG improved intent fidelity across every conflict scenario while preserving a semantic relevance scaffold. Edge-removal experiments confirmed that graph relationships mattered most when content and intent diverged.</p>
        <p class="research-method">The paper was accepted to NGEN-AI 2026 for publication in Springer proceedings. The work received Ramapo College&rsquo;s Best Research Award and was presented at the Ramapo DMC Fair and Scholar&rsquo;s Day.</p>
        <p class="research-method" style="margin-bottom:0"><a href="https://github.com/Prashant002-1/knowledge-graph-retrieval-with-affective-grounding" class="card-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KRAG on GitHub &rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="research-stat-block">
        <div class="research-stat reveal">
          <div class="stat-value">1,600</div>
          <div class="stat-label">controlled trials across agreement and intent-content conflict</div>
        </div>
        <div class="research-stat reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <div class="stat-value">6 / 6</div>
          <div class="stat-label">conflict scenarios with improved intent fidelity</div>
        </div>
        <div class="research-stat reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <div class="stat-value">521 / 800</div>
          <div class="stat-label">conflict trials with a jointly relevant top-ten result, versus 263 / 800 for Vector-RAG</div>
        </div>
        <div class="research-stat reveal reveal-delay-3">
          <div class="stat-value">2.3&times;</div>
          <div class="stat-label">stronger rank impact from emotion-edge evidence under conflict</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
